
@attribute [Route(GlobalValues.Path_Tabs_Overview)]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Page_Title_Tabs_Overview_Test</PageTitle>

<section class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Class @GlobalValues.Info_Box_Coloured_Modifier">
    <h1 class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Heading_Class">Tabs Overview & Tests</h1>

    <p>
        The Tabs component is used to group different but related content, allowing users to navigate between views (tab panels) without leaving the page.
    </p>
    <p>
        The componnet is made up of three parts, the Tab List, the Tabs and the Tab Panel. The Tab List holds the Tabs, and the Tabs are used to activate the Tab Panel to show its content. 
    </p>
    <p>
        Activation of a Tab Panel can be either automatic, whereby the content is displayed when the Tab recieves focus, or via manual activation requireing the user to press the <kbd>Enter or Space</kbd> key
        whilst on a focused Tab. These activation modes are set by the developer.
    </p>
    <p>
        There are two Tabs Compoments below, one set to use automatic activation the other to manual.
    </p>
    <p>
        <b>Released: </b>Current version <b>v1.0.0</b> See the documentation site for more information: <a target="_blank" class="@GlobalValues.Link_Class" href="@GlobalValues.Site_Link_Docs_Tabs">Toggletip documentation (opens in new window)</a>
    </p>
</section>

<section class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Class">

    <h2 class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Heading_Class">Information & instructions</h2>
    <p>
        Below are two tabs components, the first uses automatic activation for displaying the tabs, the second uses manual activation.
    </p>
    <p>
        Visit either or both. Using the keys as described below navigate the tabs and ensure that the panel content is availabe for the selected tab. 
    </p>
    <p>
        Each tab panel content has a heading followed by Lorem Ipsum text with no focusable elements.
    </p>
    <h2 id="tabs-keyboard" class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Heading_Class">Keyboard interaction</h2>
    <ul aria-labelledby="tabs-keyboard">
        <li>
            <kbd>Tab</kbd> - when focus moves into the tab list, places focus on the active tab element
            <br />When the tab list contains the focus, moves focus to the next element in the page tab sequence outside the tablist, which is the
            tabpanel unless the first element containing meaningful content inside the tabpanel is focusable.
        </li>
        <li><kbd>Left Arrow</kbd> - moves focus to the previous tab. If the focus is on the first tab, moves focus to the last tab.</li>
        <li><kbd>Right Arrow</kbd> - moves focus to the next tab. If the focus is on the last tab, moves focus to the first tab.</li>
        <li><kbd>Space or Enter</kbd> - activates the tab if it was not activated automatically on focus..</li>
        <li><kbd>Home</kbd> - moves focus to the first tab.</li>
        <li><kbd>End</kbd> - moves focus to the last tab..</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Class">

    <h3 class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Heading_Class">Expectations</h3>

    <ul>
        <li>
            Tabbing to the Tabs component should set focus on the current, selected tab.
        </li>
        <li>
            The left and right arrow keys should move the focus to the previous or next tab respectively, with the home and end keys setting focus to the first and last tabs respectively.
        </li>
        <li>
            The automatic tab panel activation should show the content on focus with screen reader users be advised that the tab is selected.
        </li>
        <li>
            For manual activation, using the enter or space key should activate the tab panel with the content being displayed and screen reader users being advised that the tab is selected.
        </li>
        <li>
            As each tab panel content has no focussable elements, pressing the tab key on a selected tab should set focus to the tab panel itself.
            Pressing the tab key again should take you to the next focusable element on the page.
        </li>
        <li>
            Voice control users should be able to select and navigate tabs by using the visible accessible name and saying the assoicated command and name, such as click Food One, focus Travel One.  
        </li>
    </ul>
</section>
